From 4d996f29f9bea0dc216930a9d4097b9d612de0f8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 02:54:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(allwinner): offer CPU_SUSPEND natively on the H616

The H616 has no SCP, so the native PSCI ops offer no CPU_SUSPEND and
Linux has no idle state beyond WFI.

Add SUNXI_NATIVE_CPU_SUSPEND: core-level CPU_SUSPEND through the
CPUIDLE block that CPU_OFF already uses. A core's wake bit is set when
it comes online and cleared at CPU_OFF, never on the idle path. All
cores are set to AArch64 once at setup, so a power-cycled core 0 does
not restart in the BROM.

Backport of the version under upstream review to lts-v2.14.11.

Link: https://review.trustedfirmware.org/c/TF-A/trusted-firmware-a/+/56325
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
